[voice path="res://Assets/Audio/VA/Sutherland/ReadsLetter.mp3" volume="-5.0"]
Narrator: 01/27\
I don't think I'll ever forget this day... Not for as long as I live.\
This morning I was terrified, hands shaking, heart pounding louder than the sea outside.\
I kept wondering if I was even ready... If I could ever be a father that she deserves.\
But then I saw her.\
So small, so warm... And the moment I held her, ghe fear just... Broke apart.\
Like the waves hitting the rocks and turning soft again.\
I looked at her tiny fingers, at the way she calmed down when I whispered her name, and I swear something changed in me.\
A light turned on somewhere I didn't even know exsited.\
I'm still nervous, God knows I am, But I've never been this happy in my life.\
If I ever lose my way in the years ahead, I hope I remember today.\
27th of January\
The day my life found its purpose.